    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my 2018 civic makes this loud squealing noise whenever i step on the gas to accelerate. i think it might be a belt issue but i'm not sure. can u explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why it would make that kind of sound if it's going bad?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt is a long, ribbed belt that transfers power from the engine's crankshaft to various accessories like the alternator, power steering pump, and water pump. When this belt starts to fail—perhaps due to glazing, fraying, or tension issues—it can slip on one of the pulleys, causing that distinct squealing noise, especially under the increased load of acceleration. Replacing this belt is a common and usually cost-effective way to resolve the sound if that is the source of your problem.",
      "source": "target",
