      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While belt issues can sometimes seem random, there is usually a pattern related to environmental or wear factors. Factors like temperature changes, engine vibrations, or debris accumulating on the belt can cause subtle degradation that leads to intermittent problems. However, a belt that is already cracked will likely continue to fail unpredictably, so regular inspection is key to catching the pattern before a complete breakdown.",
